            <ArticleTitle>[Nerve affection in connection with bloodletting II. Four case reports].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>147-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Four blood donors with persistent pain and dysfunction of the upper extremity after venepuncture are presented. Physical examinations identified median nerve-affections in all and additionally a varying involvement of other nerves in the elbow region. Such complications appear to have developed following to a vascular lesion. They are rare but potentially disabling and should be known in blood banks and clinical departments to which these patients are referred.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
